{% doc %}
  Formats a price the same way `| money` does, except for EUR (the Slovenian
  market), where the client wants the € symbol placed after the amount instead
  of before it.

  This can't be solved with Settings > General > Change currency formatting:
  that setting is one shared template used for every currency the shop sells
  in, Shopify just swaps in the right symbol and code. Editing it to move the
  € after the amount would also move the $ after the amount for the US/Canada
  market, which isn't wanted. So the EUR-only placement is handled here
  instead, and every other currency keeps using the store's own setting
  untouched.

  @param {number} amount - A price in the shop's smallest currency unit (cents), e.g. variant.price
  @param {boolean} [trim_zeros] - Drop a trailing .00, like money_without_trailing_zeros. Ignored for EUR, which always shows 2 decimals (standard for it).
{% enddoc %}
{%- if localization.country.currency.iso_code == 'EUR' -%}
  {{- amount | money_without_currency -}}&nbsp;€
{%- elsif trim_zeros -%}
  {{- amount | money_without_trailing_zeros -}}
{%- else -%}
  {{- amount | money -}}
{%- endif -%}
